$ and ${\\int }_{5}^{-5}6\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=18.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{-5}^{12}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{-5}6\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =18 \\\\ 6{\\int }_{5}^{-5}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =18 \\\\ -6{\\int }_{-5}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =18 \\\\ {\\int }_{-5}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5}^{12}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-5}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{5}^{12}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3+12 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-4725/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d752aac-6187-595d-8818-b0179fd7380e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-4725"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
